---
import ProductLayout from '../../layouts/ProductLayout.astro';
import WhatIDid from '../../components/WhatIDid.astro';
import Video from '../../components/Video.astro';
---
<ProductLayout
  slug="lyft"
  eyebrow="Competition · Management 1000 case competition"
  title="Lyft Explore"
  tagline="A feature concept that turns <strong>every bike ride into a city adventure</strong>, built on infrastructure Lyft already owns."
  hero="/images/lyft/hero.webp"
  heroAlt="Lyft Explore logo with a pink gem and two leaderboard screens"
  links={[['View the pitch deck →', 'https://gowustl-my.sharepoint.com/:p:/g/personal/joselyn_wustl_edu/IQAgulBupaGSQJfH5YM6-W8MAcLyqi0HsYOm8b-gLzve34E?e=NjrXkf']]}
  overview={[['Context', 'Class case competition'], ['Deliverable', 'Pitch deck + feature concept'], ['Tools', 'Canva, PowerPoint, Video Star'], ['Team', 'Team project']]}
>
  <WhatIDid heading='Ideas, slides, every mockup.' items={[
    ['Headed ideation', 'Led our brainstorm through <strong>rewards and car-perk ideas</strong> before we landed on gamified exploration.'],
    ['Designed the slides', 'Built the <a href="https://gowustl-my.sharepoint.com/:p:/g/personal/joselyn_wustl_edu/IQAgulBupaGSQJfH5YM6-W8MAcLyqi0HsYOm8b-gLzve34E?e=NjrXkf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">pitch deck ↗</a>: the story, the visuals and the business case.'],
    ['Made every mockup', 'The <strong>app screens</strong>, <strong>dock kiosk</strong>, <strong>handlebar screen</strong>, billboard and campaign visuals.'],
  ]} />

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>Why this problem</h2>
    <p class="pull">We wanted a <em>creative</em> answer to a real problem Lyft faces, and to help them stand out where Uber isn’t the default: <span class="hl">bikes and scooters</span>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>Research</h2>
    <p class="lead">Start with the business.</p>
    <p>I read Lyft’s <strong>10-K filings</strong>, micromobility market data, and <strong>Gen Z research</strong> before sketching anything.</p>
    <div class="band bigstats">
      <div><b>2</b><span>rides per bike, per day</span></div>
      <div><b>$9.61B</b><span>micromobility market by 2030, and no one owns it</span></div>
      <div><b>65%</b><span>of Pokémon GO players are 18 to 34</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="learn"><b>What I learned</b><p>Read the filings first. The numbers showed me the gap before any idea did.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter tinted">
    <h2>Ideation</h2>
    <p class="lead">The ideas we threw out.</p>
    <p>It took time. We explored the obvious answers first, but <strong>something was missing</strong>.</p>
    <ol class="band ideas" style="--n:3">
      <li class="out"><b>Rewards program</b><span>Lyft already runs one.</span></li>
      <li class="out"><b>New car perks</b><span>Rideshare, where Uber already competes.</span></li>
      <li class="kept"><b>Gamified exploration</b><span>Inspired by <strong>gamification trends</strong>. This is where it clicked.</span></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="learn"><b>What I learned</b><p>Good ideas take time. Ruling out the obvious ones showed us what was missing.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>The wedge</h2>
    <p class="lead">Don’t compete on bikes.</p>
    <p>Lime and Bird offer the <strong>same bikes, maps, and prices</strong>. Lyft stands for <strong>community and exploration</strong>, so I built on that.</p>
    <figure class="band">
      <img src="/images/lyft/moodboard.webp" alt="Mood board: Pokémon GO map, Strava leaderboard, Lyft Media event icons, Nike Run Club leaderboard, and a hidden gem video thumbnail" loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption>Inspiration: <strong>Pokémon GO</strong>, <strong>Strava</strong>, <strong>Snap Map</strong>, and Lyft Media’s own event mode.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="learn"><b>What I learned</b><p>You can’t win on features alone. Build on what the brand already stands for.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter tinted">
    <h2>The solution</h2>
    <p class="lead">Every ride is a hidden gem.</p>
    <p>Lyft Explore lives inside the <strong>existing Lyft map</strong>. No new app, no new hardware.</p>
    <figure class="band">
      <img src="/images/lyft/evolution.webp" alt="Three phones: today's Lyft bikes map, the gem concept map, and the final dark map with a sponsored gem" loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption><strong>Today’s map</strong> → <strong>gem concept</strong> → <strong>final</strong> dark map with a sponsored spot.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <ol class="band decisions">
      <li><i>1</i><div><b>Gem Pinpoints</b><span>Sponsored and community hot spots, using the <strong>icon system Lyft Media already runs</strong>.</span></div></li>
      <li><i>2</i><div><b>Regional leaderboard</b><span>Riders compete for <strong>Lyft credit</strong>: $50, $30, $15. Sponsors can add prizes.</span></div></li>
      <li><i>3</i><div><b>Points that plug in</b><span>An optional layer that joins <strong>Lyft Rewards</strong> instead of running separately.</span></div></li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="band">
      <img src="/images/lyft/final-screens.webp" alt="Final screens: a brand-sponsored leaderboard, the Lyft leaderboard, and the map with a 300-point gem" loading="lazy" />
    </figure>
    <div class="band cols">
      <figure><img src="/images/lyft/kiosk-map.webp" alt="Bike dock kiosk showing a sponsored leaderboard next to the app map" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>On the <strong>dock kiosk</strong></figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/lyft/handlebar.webp" alt="Lyft bike handlebar screen showing the gem map" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>On the <strong>handlebar screen</strong></figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <div class="band mycall">
      <h3>The question I asked myself</h3>
      <p class="pull">Won’t gamification keep people glued to their phones?</p>
      <p class="pull answer">The app is the guide, not the destination. Points only come from <span class="hl">riding to real places</span>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="learn"><b>What I learned</b><p>Designing inside real infrastructure is harder, and far more convincing.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>Campaign</h2>
    <p class="lead">On the street and in the feed.</p>
    <p><strong>Billboards</strong> near the docks, plus <strong>creator-style video</strong> that shows what a ride feels like.</p>
    <div class="band cols">
      <figure><img src="/images/lyft/campaign.webp" alt="Campaign key visual: Every ride is a hidden gem, with a Lyft scooter" loading="lazy" /></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/lyft/billboard.webp" alt="Digital billboard mockup of the campaign outside a building" loading="lazy" /></figure>
    </div>
    <div class="band vids">
      <Video name="lyft-ride-concept" label="Concept video: riders exploring the city while a gem floats overhead and the leaderboard updates" caption="How we imagine a ride." />
      <Video name="lyft-explore-with-me" frame="bare" label="Creator-style social video: Come explore with me, Lyft Explore edition" caption="Come explore with me." />
    </div>
    <div class="learn"><b>What I learned</b><p>A feature needs a story before anyone will use it.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter tinted">
    <h2>Results</h2>
    <p class="lead">The business case.</p>
    <div class="band bigstats">
      <div><b>720%</b><span>projected ROI</span></div>
      <div><b>87.7%</b><span>profit margin</span></div>
      <div><b>$317M</b><span>5-year profit, up from $213M</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="note">Projected in Excel and Google Sheets using Divvy bike data and Lyft’s segment revenue.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>What I learned</h2>
    <ol class="band takeaways-big" style="max-width:var(--text)">
      <li>Rule out the obvious ideas before settling.</li>
      <li>Build on what the brand already stands for.</li>
      <li>Test with real riders next time. This ran on secondary research.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</ProductLayout>

<style>
  .vids { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr; gap: 28px; align-items: center; text-align: left; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .vids { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
